<title>USA: Lukens Medical gets FDA nod for product.</title>
<headline>Lukens Medical gets FDA nod for product.</headline>
<dateline>ALBUQUERQUE, N.M. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lukens Medical Corp said on Tuesday it received U.S. Food and Drug Administration clearance for its new synthetic, absorbable suture material, which it will put on the market in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The company estimates the market for synthetic absorbable sutures worldwide to exceed $500 million annually.</p>
<p>The new suture will be marketed worldwide under the tradename PGA(TM). It is used in most surgical procedures, and heavily used in gynecology, orthopedics and general surgery.</p>
<p>Lukens is a disposable medical products company addressing global markets in sutures, diagnostics and other products.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
